WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.351 --> 00:00:01.743
(gentle instrumental music)

00:00:01.743 --> 00:00:03.918
- When a patient first
comes to our office,

00:00:03.918 --> 00:00:08.082
they feel a little self-conscious
about the way they look,

00:00:08.082 --> 00:00:10.889
or they don't wanna
look people eye to eye.

00:00:10.889 --> 00:00:12.169
People always think,

00:00:12.169 --> 00:00:14.470
"I'm just doing this
for cosmetic reasons,"

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:16.939
but actually it's the
restoration of the person.

00:00:16.939 --> 00:00:20.000
(gentle instrumental music)

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.318
I'm an ocularist.

00:00:21.318 --> 00:00:22.756
That is someone that fits and fabricates

00:00:22.756 --> 00:00:24.285
artificial eyes for people.

00:00:24.285 --> 00:00:25.800
(gentle instrumental music)

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.525
During the surgery to remove your eye,

00:00:27.525 --> 00:00:30.355
the doctors place an
implant in the muscle crown,

00:00:30.355 --> 00:00:32.907
so we fit a concave, convex shape

00:00:32.907 --> 00:00:36.804
that sits like a contact
lens on the implant.

00:00:36.804 --> 00:00:38.481
It is an art form.

00:00:38.481 --> 00:00:40.380
We do everything by hand.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:42.129
First we take an impression.

00:00:42.129 --> 00:00:44.915
This gives us an imprint
of the exact structures

00:00:44.915 --> 00:00:46.877
behind the eyelids.

00:00:46.877 --> 00:00:49.038
Painting is very challenging.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:51.269
Everything starts from a black disk,

00:00:51.269 --> 00:00:53.323
and everything is painted on top of that.

00:00:53.323 --> 00:00:56.169
It's very difficult to
match the iris color.

00:00:56.169 --> 00:00:58.289
No two people have the same color,

00:00:58.289 --> 00:00:59.775
so we'll sit there with a paint brush,

00:00:59.775 --> 00:01:02.420
and we'll paint different structures,

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:04.842
dots, dashes, striations,

00:01:04.842 --> 00:01:06.861
overlay that with different hues

00:01:06.861 --> 00:01:09.395
or different saturations of color

00:01:09.395 --> 00:01:10.914
to give it the three dimensional effect

00:01:10.914 --> 00:01:13.749
that we see in people's natural eyes.

00:01:13.749 --> 00:01:15.967
(gentle instrumental music)

00:01:15.967 --> 00:01:17.758
Part of what makes it look natural

00:01:17.758 --> 00:01:20.031
is to have the sparkle in your eye.

00:01:20.031 --> 00:01:22.378
We do that with fine polishing

00:01:22.378 --> 00:01:25.823
and fine tuning the curves
of the artificial eye.

00:01:25.823 --> 00:01:28.291
The part I most like about
fabricating a prosthesis

00:01:28.291 --> 00:01:29.952
is when I've finished it,

00:01:29.952 --> 00:01:30.852
and I look at it,

00:01:30.852 --> 00:01:34.345
and I see the illusion
that I've just created.

00:01:34.345 --> 00:01:35.895
When somebody loses their eye,

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:37.512
sometimes they feel like they've lost

00:01:37.512 --> 00:01:40.243
part of their self-being.

00:01:40.243 --> 00:01:41.711
We make them feel whole again

00:01:41.711 --> 00:01:43.787
and confident to take on the world.

00:01:43.787 --> 00:01:47.454
(gentle instrumental music)

